@startuml
actor Student
participant BookingService
participant BookingRepository
Student -> BookingService: requestBooking(roomId, startTime, endTime)
BookingService -> BookingService: validateTimeRange(startTime, endTime) (R1)
alt invalid time range
  BookingService --> Student: reject booking (R1)
else valid time range
  BookingService -> BookingRepository: isRoomBlocked(roomId) (R3)
  BookingRepository --> BookingService: blocked status
  alt room blocked
    BookingService --> Student: reject booking (R3)
  else room unblocked
    BookingService -> BookingRepository: hasOverlappingActiveBooking(roomId, startTime, endTime) (R2)
    BookingRepository --> BookingService: overlap result
    alt overlap exists
      BookingService --> Student: reject booking (R2)
    else room available
      BookingService -> BookingRepository: saveBooking(roomId, startTime, endTime)
      BookingRepository --> BookingService: booking created
      BookingService --> Student: send successful booking confirmation (R4)
    end
  end
end
note over BookingService
  R1 checks a future start and a positive duration of at most two hours.
  R2 treats bookings as half-open intervals; touching endpoints do not overlap.
  Blocking a room prevents new bookings and does not cancel existing bookings.
  BookingService validates and coordinates; BookingRepository checks and stores bookings.
end note
@enduml
